            id: "training-policy",
            title: "Training and Development",
            content: "The Company will ensure through its recruitment that only employees with the physical and mental attributes for the task are engaged. The Directors will ensure that before any employee is allowed to operate unsupervised, they will have been given adequate instruction and training to complete the task efficiently and safely.\n\n<ol>\n<li>Risk assessment of the operation with respect to the operator, direct and indirect employees and members of the public.</li>\n<li>A method statement or working procedure will be devised with the operative involved.</li>\n<li>A training programme will be devised giving clear instruction on the work tasks to be completed.</li>\n<li>The operative will be asked to confirm that he/she has understood the written and/or verbal communications.</li>\n<li>The operative will be monitored performing the procedure and will not be allowed to work unsupervised until the relevant manager is satisfied that he/she can complete the work in accordance with the procedure.</li>\n<li>All operatives will be monitored on a random basis to ensure that they continue to operate to the agreed procedure.</li>\n<li>Experienced or expert instructors, which depending upon the task may be external to the company, will provide training.</li>\n<li>A record will be maintained of the training carried out.</li>\n<li>After an accident, incident or near miss, the staff member(s) involved will be interviewed by the relevant manager and if deemed necessary, further training given before they are permitted to recommence working on that task.</li>\n<li>Staff who have a poor command of English may be expected to take English language lessons provided by the company.</li>\n<li>The company philosophy is that employees who have shown loyalty, reliability and commitment, will be invited to undertake external training to benefit them and the company.</li>\n<li>Only employees who have had certificated external training will be permitted to use mobile plant, i.e. loading shovels, excavators and forklifts.</li>\n<li>Staff who have demonstrated an aptitude for vehicle driving may be invited to take HGV driving course.</li>\n<li>Before being offered training by an external trainer, the employee must have demonstrated they are reliable, conscientious, a safe worker and worthy of career advancement.</li>\n<li>Where external training is offered to a member of staff that they would subsequently be able to use at another employer e.g. HGV or Forklift truck driver, they will be required to reimburse the company for the training cost if they leave within two years of the date they completed their training.</li>\n</ol>"
